# Reuse local tooling (do not re-download)

Before downloading, installing, or re-fetching any toolchain or dependency distribution:

1. Check whether it already exists on this machine and use it.
2. Prefer the real user caches over Cursor sandbox cache paths.
3. Do not wipe caches, reinstall JDKs/SDKs, or re-download Gradle/npm packages “to be safe.”

## Known local installs (this machine)

- Gradle user home: `C:\Users\K\.gradle` (distribution `gradle-8.11.1` already cached)
- Android build toolchain: `%LOCALAPPDATA%\AndroidBuild` (JDK 17 + Android SDK) via `deploy\android\build-android.ps1`
- Android APK script: `deploy\android\build-android.ps1` (sets `JAVA_HOME` / `ANDROID_HOME`)

## Android Gradle builds

When running Gradle from the agent, **force**:

```powershell
$env:GRADLE_USER_HOME = "C:\Users\K\.gradle"
```

Cursor may set `GRADLE_USER_HOME` to a sandbox cache under `%TEMP%\cursor-sandbox-cache\...`; that causes a useless re-download of Gradle. Override it before `gradlew` / `build-android.ps1`.

If a download appears stuck, inspect locks under `.gradle\wrapper\dists` and the effective `GRADLE_USER_HOME` first — do not start a fresh install.
